The baseline uses `x * x`, which counts as a ct_ct_mul. The DSL says `square(c)` is also a ciphertext-ciphertext multiplication, but CHEHAB may lower it differently, for example with a cheaper relinearization path. The circuit would then differ from the baseline (square=1 instead of ct_ct_mul=1), so I'll try `square(x)`.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext y = square(x);
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

`x²` needs at least one ciphertext-ciphertext multiplication with relinearization and rescale. There is no plaintext input to exploit and no rotation to save, so I don't see a cheaper circuit than the baseline. The only variant I can think of that changes the circuit is `(x + x) * x - x * x`, which uses two multiplications and is strictly worse. I'll resubmit the minimal form below as a sanity check, and I don't expect it to win.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext y = x * x;
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

I still don't see a cheaper circuit: one ct-ct multiply is the minimum for x², and any rewrite only adds work. Here is a structurally different but equivalent form, which I expect to be slower and which is mainly a probe of how CHEHAB treats it.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext a = x + x;
  Ciphertext y = a * x - x * x;
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

I can't find a circuit cheaper than the baseline. Attempt 3 confirmed that extra multiplications double the time (129.69 ms against 64.23 ms). A single ct-ct multiply with its relinearization and rescale is the minimum for x², because there are no plaintext inputs, rotations or other terms to trade away. I'm keeping the best kernel, which is the baseline.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext y = x * x;
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

I have no cheaper circuit to propose. The baseline's single multiply with relinearization and rescale is the minimum for x², and every structural change I can construct adds operations. I'm resubmitting the same kernel, so it will be reported as identical to the baseline.

```cpp
